1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,046
At the 1904 Olympics,

2
00:00:02,336 --> 00:00:03,718
Fred Lorz was the first

3
00:00:03,864 --> 00:00:04,664
marathon runner

4
00:00:04,773 --> 00:00:05,900
across the finish line.

5
00:00:06,409 --> 00:00:07,646
But he didn't win.

6
00:00:08,082 --> 00:00:09,536
Exhausted during the race,

7
00:00:09,827 --> 00:00:11,209
Lorz dropped out and got

8
00:00:11,282 --> 00:00:12,373
into a car heading back

9
00:00:12,446 --> 00:00:13,100
to the stadium.

10
00:00:13,536 --> 00:00:15,136
Then the car broke down.

11
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:16,082
He got out,

12
00:00:16,373 --> 00:00:17,464
ran the rest of the way,

13
00:00:17,682 --> 00:00:18,555
and reached the finish

14
00:00:18,627 --> 00:00:19,936
before the other runners.

15
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:21,318
Once officials learned

16
00:00:21,391 --> 00:00:22,046
he had travelled

17
00:00:22,118 --> 00:00:23,355
part of the course by car,

18
00:00:23,646 --> 00:00:25,027
Lorz was disqualified.

19
00:00:25,391 --> 00:00:26,409
Thomas Hicks became

20
00:00:26,446 --> 00:00:27,355
the Olympic champion.

21
00:00:27,791 --> 00:00:29,173
The next year, Lorz

22
00:00:29,246 --> 00:00:30,555
won the Boston Marathon.
